														</div>
			</div>
			<div class="content" id="post-content-1413862">
									

<p>Not much to say that's already been said, but I'm really liking this.</p>
<p>This is probably just me personally, but&#8230;</p>
<div class="collapsible-block">
<div class="collapsible-block-folded"><a class="collapsible-block-link" href="javascript:;">+&nbsp;spoilers</a></div>
<div class="collapsible-block-unfolded" style="display:none">
<div class="collapsible-block-unfolded-link"><a class="collapsible-block-link" href="javascript:;">-&nbsp;spoilers</a></div>
<div class="collapsible-block-content">
<p>I can't help but feel that maybe the nest could have been a bit more horrifying. Maybe instead of ripping victims' hearts out, the entities could have just dragged victims inside the farmhouse. Then the nest could have been revealed to be an &quot;eternal suffering&quot; kind of deal where the victims were set up in a undoubtedly painful process where they were constantly &quot;birthing&quot; new entities forever. Maybe it could have been noted that once an agent who was being dragged shot him/herself before the entity entered the farmhouse, but the document reveals they just brought him/her back to life somehow and he/she's integrated in the &quot;reproductive process&quot; just like the others. This is fairly cliche, I know. I'm just rambling on about what would personally hit me harder.</p>
</div>
</div>
</div>
<p>What's here definitely works though, and I upvoted regardless. Great work, Mr. Mann.</p>

